 About: Processes                                                     
   PID             Process ID, a number the OS gives each running     
                   process. Use it with `taskman kill <pid>`. IDs are 
                   reused after a process exits.                      
   NAME            The program's executable name. Grouping (z)        
                   combines processes with the same name, e.g.        
                   "chrome (31)", summing their CPU and memory.       
   USER            The account the process runs as. Blank usually     
                   means a system account you can't inspect without   
                   admin rights.                                      
   CPU%            Share of total CPU capacity used since the last    
                   refresh. Normalized (default): 100% means every    
                   core is busy, like Task Manager. Per-core (c):     
